---
// ROUND 05 — THE LIVE FRONTIER (the honest closer, rebuilt 2026-06-11).
//
// The old beat (a vocal/body "defect", "not shipped", a blind pipeline as future
// roadmap) is retired: the blind loop now EXISTS and runs decision-grade. The
// current story is three tight beats:
//   the proof  — processing beats raw, but per-SECTION: verse wants it on, drop
//                wants it off; a hard-cut hybrid beat both straight-through masters.
//                A master no single chain could make.
//   the loop   — no universal chain + meters fight the ears, so the engine stopped
//                guessing and started ASKING: it models its own uncertainty, serves
//                the single most-useful blind round, takes the vote, updates, repeats.
//   the frontier — the falsifiable promise: uncertainty falls round-over-round, so the
//                rounds it serves drift toward genuine toss-ups — the live frontier.
//
// 100% server-rendered, visible with NO JS (the honest readout must never hide behind
// a click). All visuals are static inline SVG, so there's no IO/scroll/rAF to throttle,
// and reduced-motion is automatic. Rhymes with RoundFrame/TasteTrial (Round-05 header,
// the-bet line, the verdict="live" yellow). The −2 dBTP floor + the aim close it out.

// the proof: one real track, split into the two sections that disagreed.
const SECTIONS = [
  { name: "verse", won: "processed", note: "wanted it on" },
  { name: "drop", won: "raw", note: "wanted it off" },
];
// the scoreboard: the two straight-through masters vs the section-aware hybrid.
const MASTERS = [
  { label: "all processed", win: false },
  { label: "all raw", win: false },
  { label: "section-aware hybrid", win: true },
];
// the loop, three nodes on a cycle.
const LOOP = [
  { k: "asks", t: "it asks", s: "the round it's least sure of", lead: true },
  { k: "vote", t: "you vote", s: "blind · loudness-matched" },
  { k: "learn", t: "it learns", s: "updates its belief" },
];
// the frontier: average uncertainty falling round-over-round (illustrative shape).
const UNCERT = [0.92, 0.71, 0.55, 0.42, 0.33, 0.27];
---

<section class="lf" data-live-frontier>
  <header class="lf-head">
    <span class="lf-num">Round 05</span>
    <span class="lf-phase">the live frontier</span>
  </header>

  <p class="lf-belief">
    <span class="lf-belief-tag">the bet</span>
    It used to fire six masters into the dark and hope one stuck. Now it's wired to win: it asks the one thing it's least sure of, I vote blind, it learns, and it asks again.
  </p>

  <div class="lf-status">
    <span class="lf-stamp">n=1 · learning in the open</span>
    <span class="lf-stamp-cap">One builder, one set of ears, working in the open. The honesty is the credibility — the opposite of a button that overclaims and forgets you.</span>
  </div>

  <!-- BEAT 1 · the proof — section-aware beats any single chain -->
  <div class="lf-panel lf-proof-panel">
    <span class="lf-mini">the proof</span>
    <p class="lf-text">Processing beats raw — but not everywhere in a song. On one track the <b>verse</b> wanted it on and the <b>drop</b> wanted it off, every blind time. A hard-cut hybrid — processed verse, raw drop — beat <b>both</b> straight-through masters. A master no single chain could make.</p>

    <div class="lf-proofviz">
      <svg class="lf-track" viewBox="0 0 320 92" role="img" aria-label="One track split into two sections. The verse won the processed master; the drop won the raw master. The section-aware hybrid of the two beat both straight-through masters, blind, four out of four.">
        <text x="0" y="9" class="lf-cap">CantBreathe · by section</text>
        <!-- the split track lane -->
        <g transform="translate(0,16)">
          <rect class="lf-seg lf-seg-proc" x="0" y="0" width="174" height="26" rx="4" />
          <rect class="lf-seg lf-seg-raw" x="178" y="0" width="142" height="26" rx="4" />
          <text x="14" y="16" class="lf-seg-lab">verse → processed</text>
          <text x="190" y="16" class="lf-seg-lab lf-seg-lab-dim">drop → raw</text>
        </g>
        <!-- the scoreboard: two uniform masters lose, the hybrid wins -->
        <g transform="translate(0,52)" class="lf-score">
          <g>
            <text x="0" y="9" class="lf-score-lab">all processed</text>
            <rect x="120" y="2" width="120" height="7" rx="3.5" class="lf-bar lf-bar-lose" />
            <text x="318" y="9" text-anchor="end" class="lf-score-x">lost</text>
          </g>
          <g transform="translate(0,14)">
            <text x="0" y="9" class="lf-score-lab">all raw</text>
            <rect x="120" y="2" width="96" height="7" rx="3.5" class="lf-bar lf-bar-lose" />
            <text x="318" y="9" text-anchor="end" class="lf-score-x">lost</text>
          </g>
          <g transform="translate(0,28)">
            <text x="0" y="9" class="lf-score-lab lf-score-win">section-aware hybrid</text>
            <rect x="120" y="2" width="120" height="7" rx="3.5" class="lf-bar lf-bar-win" />
            <text x="318" y="9" text-anchor="end" class="lf-score-w">won · 4/4 blind</text>
          </g>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>

    {/*
      REAL-AUDIO HOOK — when Jon supplies the CantBreathe clips (uniform vs the hybrid,
      same passage, loudness-matched), a <TheBench round={r5SectionAB} /> drops in here,
      matching the BenchRound API. Ships invisible until then: no player chrome.
    */}
    <div class="lf-bench-slot" data-audio-slot="round05-section-ab" hidden></div>
  </div>

  <!-- BEAT 2 · the loop — the engine stopped guessing and started asking -->
  <div class="lf-panel lf-loop-panel">
    <span class="lf-mini">the loop</span>
    <p class="lf-text">There's no universal chain, and the meters disagree with the ears. So the engine stopped guessing and started <b>asking</b>: it models what it's least sure about, serves that one blind round, takes the vote, updates, and serves the next.</p>

    <div class="lf-loop" role="img" aria-label="A repeating loop: the engine asks the round it is least sure of, you vote blind and loudness-matched, it learns and updates its belief, then it asks again.">
      {LOOP.map((n, i) => (
        <Fragment>
          <div class:list={["lf-node", { "lf-node-lead": n.lead }]}>
            <span class="lf-node-t">{n.t}</span>
            <span class="lf-node-s">{n.s}</span>
          </div>
          {i < LOOP.length - 1 && <span class="lf-node-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>}
        </Fragment>
      ))}
      <span class="lf-loop-return" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 300 24" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M296 2 v8 a6 6 0 0 1 -6 6 H12 a6 6 0 0 1 -6 -6 V2" /><path class="lf-loop-head" d="M2 8 L6 2 L10 8" /></svg>
        <em>repeat</em>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- BEAT 3 · the frontier — the falsifiable promise, made literal -->
  <div class="lf-panel lf-frontier-panel">
    <span class="lf-mini">the frontier</span>
    <p class="lf-text">The claim I can be proven wrong on: its uncertainty has to <b>fall, round over round</b>. As it does, the rounds it serves drift toward genuine <b>toss-ups</b> — the calls it still can't make on its own. That moving edge is the live frontier.</p>

    <div class="lf-frontierviz">
      <svg class="lf-uncert" viewBox="0 0 320 104" role="img" aria-label="A chart of the engine's average uncertainty falling across six rounds, approaching a toss-up line at the bottom. The rounds it serves trend toward that frontier of genuine toss-ups.">
        <text x="0" y="9" class="lf-cap">avg. uncertainty / round &darr;</text>
        <!-- toss-up frontier line -->
        <line x1="0" y1="86" x2="268" y2="86" class="lf-tossline" />
        <text x="318" y="89" text-anchor="end" class="lf-tosslab">toss-up</text>
        {UNCERT.map((u, i) => {
          const x = 14 + i * 46;
          const h = Math.round(u * 64);
          const y = 84 - h;
          return (
            <g>
              <rect x={x} y={y} width="26" height={h} rx="3" class:list={["lf-ubar", { "lf-ubar-edge": i >= UNCERT.length - 2 }]} />
              <text x={x + 13} y="98" class="lf-uax">{`r${i + 1}`}</text>
            </g>
          );
        })}
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- the floor: the one hard number -->
  <div class="lf-floor">
    <span class="lf-floor-num">&minus;2 dBTP</span>
    <p class="lf-text">The one hard number it will stand on: a true-peak ceiling that survives streaming codecs intact, where a &minus;1 dBTP master clips after the transcode.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="lf-end">The master you'd keep over doing nothing — proven blind. Not finished. Truer every round.</p>
</section>

<style>
  .lf { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; color: #f5f1e8; }

  /* ── header + belief: rhyme RoundFrame / TasteTrial; the num is yellow to flag the
        live frontier at a glance ── */
  .lf-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .lf-num {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brand-yellow);
  }
  .lf-phase {
    font-family: "Space Grotesk Variable", "Space Grotesk", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 22px); color: #f5f1e8; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .lf-belief {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.82);
    margin: 0 0 16px; max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .lf-belief-tag {
    display: inline-block; margin-right: 9px;
    font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4); vertical-align: 1px;
  }

  /* ── the n=1 badge, worn high so honesty leads ── */
  .lf-status { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .lf-stamp {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brand-yellow); border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 9px; white-space: nowrap; transform: rotate(-3deg);
  }
  .lf-stamp-cap {
    flex: 1 1 280px; min-width: 0;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.55);
  }

  /* ── shared panel chrome — left rule yellow on the live beats ── */
  .lf-panel {
    background: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid var(--cs-line, rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.1));
    border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-top: 12px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow);
  }
  .lf-loop-panel { border-left-color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.18); }
  .lf-mini {
    display: block; margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.45);
  }
  .lf-text {
    margin: 0; max-width: 64ch;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--cs-text-muted, rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.72));
  }
  .lf-text b { color: #f5f1e8; font-weight: 600; }

  /* ── shared viz type ── */
  .lf-cap, .lf-seg-lab, .lf-score-lab, .lf-score-x, .lf-score-w, .lf-uax, .lf-tosslab {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .lf-cap { font-size: 8px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4); }

  /* BEAT 1 · the proof viz */
  .lf-proofviz { margin-top: 13px; }
  .lf-track { width: 100%; max-width: 340px; height: auto; }
  .lf-seg { stroke-width: 1; }
  .lf-seg-proc { fill: rgba(14, 196, 252, 0.16); stroke: rgba(14, 196, 252, 0.6); }
  .lf-seg-raw { fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.04); stroke: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.28); stroke-dasharray: 3 2.5; }
  .lf-seg-lab { font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; fill: #bfeeff; }
  .lf-seg-lab-dim { fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.6); }
  .lf-score-lab { font-size: 8.5px; fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.62); }
  .lf-score-win { fill: var(--brand-yellow); }
  .lf-bar { }
  .lf-bar-lose { fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.14); }
  .lf-bar-win { fill: var(--brand-yellow); }
  .lf-score-x { font-size: 8px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.34); }
  .lf-score-w { font-size: 8px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.06em; fill: var(--brand-yellow); }

  /* BEAT 2 · the loop */
  .lf-loop { display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 13px; position: relative; padding-bottom: 26px; }
  .lf-node {
    flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 120px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.14); border-radius: 6px; padding: 9px 12px;
    background: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.015);
  }
  .lf-node-lead { border-color: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.5); background: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.05); box-shadow: inset 0 0 22px -12px var(--brand-yellow); }
  .lf-node-t { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 12px; color: #f5f1e8; font-weight: 700; }
  .lf-node-lead .lf-node-t { color: var(--brand-yellow); }
  .lf-node-s { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 9.5px; line-height: 1.3; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.5); }
  .lf-node-arrow { align-self: center; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.32); font-size: 14px; flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .lf-loop-return { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; height: 22px; }
  .lf-loop-return svg { flex: 1 1 auto; height: 22px; width: 100%; fill: none; stroke: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.26); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .lf-loop-head { stroke: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.26); }
  .lf-loop-return em { flex: 0 0 auto; font-style: normal; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 8.5px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4); }

  /* BEAT 3 · the frontier */
  .lf-frontierviz { margin-top: 13px; }
  .lf-uncert { width: 100%; max-width: 340px; height: auto; }
  .lf-ubar { fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.18); }
  .lf-ubar-edge { fill: var(--brand-yellow); opacity: 0.85; }
  .lf-uax { font-size: 8px; fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.34); text-anchor: middle; }
  .lf-tossline { stroke: var(--brand-yellow); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; opacity: 0.6; }
  .lf-tosslab { font-size: 7.5px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; fill: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.7); }

  /* ── the floor: the one number ── */
  .lf-floor {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 12px; padding: 14px 16px;
    background: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid var(--cs-line, rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.1));
    border-left: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow); border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .lf-floor-num {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--brand-yellow); font-feature-settings: "tnum";
    text-shadow: 0 0 14px rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.3);
  }
  .lf-floor .lf-text { flex: 1 1 280px; }

  /* ── the aim ── */
  .lf-end {
    margin: 18px 0 0; max-width: 64ch;
    font-family: "Space Grotesk Variable", "Space Grotesk", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; color: #f5f1e8;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .lf-loop { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .lf-node-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); align-self: flex-start; margin-left: 14px; }
    .lf-loop-return { display: none; }
  }
</style>
